  "round_12_notes": [
    "Deterministic resolver follows Constitution Article XX: exact subject, domain/candidate partitioning, explicit scope-specific supersession, authority-scope precedence, preservation, dependency state, and fail-closed conflicts.",
    "resolution_facet is an optional Verdict discriminator used only when multiple scientifically distinct obligations share the same subject, axis and domain.",
    "SCOPED_SET is a generated resolver summary, not a primary scientific verdict.",
    "SCOPE_INCOMPLETE and AUTHORITY_GAP are generated resolver audit states and do not overwrite source verdicts.",
    "EVALUATES and GOVERNED_BY were already present in live relations and are now declared in the controlled vocabulary.",
    "DatasetFamily is declared because the Round-10 LRE graph already uses it for role-neutral likelihood families with no concrete dataset frozen."
  ],
  "round_5_notes": [
    "ProviderControl is structurally distinct from Observable.",
    "ForwardProduct records preauthorization/claim state independently of provider implementation.",
    "CalibrationModel records empirical fit/replay objects without implying validation.",
    "G-TH non-fitted provider closure and G-EMP fitted diagnostics are disjoint claim lanes."
  ],
  "round_6_notes": [
    "Early-universe/baryogenesis authority graph is explicit from A1/A1R through A2/A2R, A3/A3A-A3E1, BG4A/B/C/C1 and BG5A/B1/B2.",
    "Old-identity failures and branch-specific negative results are preserved when repaired successors are introduced.",
    "Structural/interface passes do not promote absent physical providers or finite baryogenesis execution.",
    "Lambda_MSbar,H is an accepted theory-parameter class with no numerical value, range or prior selected.",
    "BG5B2A admits only a restricted weak-sphaleron rate ingredient; it is not a complete visible-sector transport provider."
  ],
